    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d696">

                <pb facs="0817" n="807" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg807"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.796A/4–1248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-05-14T17:00:00-04:00">May 14, 1948—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>905. Re Condes 187 Apr 12.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d696-f1"/> Dept and CAA holding
                    preliminary discussions re staff of mission and procurement of equipment. More
                    definite info will be forwarded Consulate General within 2 or 3 weeks. Sent
                    Shanghai as Dept’s 905 repeated Nanking as 727.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
